From 73f822839830eaac84867f8da14640b942161f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:50:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid printf formatting when copying short tokenizer input

The one-client PostgreSQL SELECT 1 profile identifies snprintf and its
stdio formatting machinery on the request-forwarding path. Existing CPU
call stacks place snprintf under legacy_command_type -> tokenizer. The
input length has already been computed, and the stack-buffer branch only
accepts inputs of at most 127 bytes into its 128-byte buffer.

Copy the known bytes and their terminating NUL directly with memcpy.
Keep heap allocation for longer inputs, token splitting, ownership,
empty-token handling, digest generation, query classification and query
routing behavior unchanged. This is shared tokenizer code; it is not a
SELECT 1 special case or a change to query-digest settings.

Validation before commit: optimized ProxySQL build succeeded; an isolated
differential check of the actual old/new tokenizer implementations matched
31,694 cases including NULL input, embedded terminators, both empty-token
modes, varied delimiters and the 127/128-byte allocation boundary. No
repository test was changed. Matching unprofiled one-client benchmark and
phase-correlated profile validation follow this implementation commit.
---
 lib/c_tokenizer.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp b/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
index 63419bf0b..72c889c79 100644
--- a/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
+++ b/lib/c_tokenizer.cpp
@@ -32,7 +32,9 @@ void tokenizer(tokenizer_t *result, const char* s, const char* delimiters, int e
 		if (result->s_length > (PROXYSQL_TOKENIZER_BUFFSIZE-1)) {
 			result->s = strdup(s);
 		} else {
-			snprintf(result->buffer, sizeof(result->buffer), "%.*s", (int)result->s_length, s);
+			// The length is already known and fits, including the terminator.
+			// Avoid invoking printf formatting for this per-query text copy.
+			memcpy(result->buffer, s, result->s_length + 1);
 			result->s = result->buffer;
 		}
 		}
